<div class="row">
  <div class="col-md-9 contents">
    <div class="page-header">
    <h1>Create a mixing distribution object</h1>
    <small class="dont-index">Source: <a href='https://github.com/dm13450/dirichletprocess/blob/master/R/mixing_distribution.R'><code>R/mixing_distribution.R</code></a></small>
    <div class="hidden name"><code>MixingDistribution.Rd</code></div>
    </div>

    <div class="ref-description">
    
    <p>The constructor function for a mixing distribution object.
Use this function to prepare an object for use with the appropriate distribution functions.</p>
    
    </div>

    <pre class="usage"><span class='fu'>MixingDistribution</span>(<span class='kw'>distribution</span>, <span class='kw'>priorParameters</span>, <span class='kw'>conjugate</span>,
  mhStepSize = <span class='kw'>NULL</span>, hyperPriorParameters = <span class='kw'>NULL</span>)</pre>
    
    <h2 class="hasAnchor" id="arguments"><a class="anchor" href="#arguments"></a>Arguments</h2>
    <table class="ref-arguments">
    <colgroup><col class="name" /><col class="desc" /></colgroup>
    <tr>
      <th>distribution</th>
      <td><p>The name of the distribution mixture</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th>priorParameters</th>
      <td><p>The prior parameters</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th>conjugate</th>
      <td><p>Whether the prior is conjugate to the Likelihood.</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th>mhStepSize</th>
      <td><p>The scale of the proposal parameter for the Metropolis Hastings algorithm. Not needed for conjugate mixtures.</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th>hyperPriorParameters</th>
      <td><p>Vector of hyperPriorParameters for the distribution.</p></td>
    </tr>
    </table>
    

